0015:     - The two foreground colors have distinct pixel counts.
0016: 
0017:     Rule
0018:     - Ignore marker positions and use only the two foreground counts.
0019:     - Make a 16-by-16 background canvas, fill a bottom-left red rectangle whose height is the smaller count and width is the larger count.
0020:     - Paint yellow pixels along the two rising 45-degree diagonals from the rectangle's bottom-left and bottom-right corners.
0021: 
0022:     Key insight
0023:     - The marker colors and positions vary between examples; their counts alone determine the output rectangle dimensions.
